  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Nifurpirinol may interact with PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L2 through a series of molecular targets. Specifically, Nifurpirinol is shown to target UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B15, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including Cespitularin C and Euphoscopin A. These compounds are all linked to the same target, PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L2. The scores for these relationships are consistent, with a final score of 0.5396, indicating a moderate level of confidence in the observed interactions. The mechanism appears to involve the UDP-glucuronosyltransferase enzymes, which are involved in drug metabolism and may play a role in the activation or inhibition of the kinase target. The evidence suggests a potential pathway where Nifurpirinol could influence the activity of CDC2L2 through its interaction with these enzymes, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
